  "notes": "Transcribed from the official ARC 'Culinary Arts/ Restaurant Management Certificate (Full Time)' program roadmap, Catalog 2026-27, published July 14, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7395/PublishedPdf). Total Units 46.5 = 13+12.5+12+9 (semester sums verified). tccns mirrors ARC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS). The production courses HM 370, 375, and 380 require students to work in the Oak Cafe or Oak Cafe bakery and require HM 498 work experience as a corequisite course. HM 370 and 380 cannot be taken in the same semester. HM 320 is offered during the 1st 8 weeks of the semester; HM 325 is offered during the 2nd 8 weeks. This map shows one possible way to finish the program in two years; see a counselor to adjust the coursework. The skills acquired through this certificate prepare students to work in the restaurant industry, in a kitchen, dining room, or other foodservice or entry-level hospitality position; students are encouraged to begin working prior to graduation. HM 498 Work Experience in Hospitality Management is taken in two semesters with different credit values, exactly as the official program map prints it.",
